  "notes": [
    "Irregular reflexive -AR verb — inherits every irregularity of *dar* (irregular yo form *doy*, irregular preterite *di/diste/dio...*, and the subjunctive forms built on *dé/des/dé/demos/den*, which keep a written accent on *dé* only when it stands alone to distinguish it from the preposition *de*)",
    "Affirmative imperative: *date* and *dense* need no written accent since the natural stress already falls correctly by default Spanish stress rules; *démonos* needs one because without it the stress would shift to the wrong syllable (nosotros drops the final -s before attaching -nos: *demos* → *demo* + *nos* → *démonos*)",
    "Past participle: *dado* (regular)",
    "Two very different meanings: literal **\"to give oneself/each other\"** — *se dieron la mano* (they shook hands) — and the far more common idiomatic **\"to happen/occur\"** or **\"to turn out to be\"** — *se dio una oportunidad única* (a unique opportunity arose), *se le dan bien los idiomas* (he/she is good at languages)",
    "Common set phrases: *darse cuenta (de)* = to realize, *darse prisa* = to hurry up, *darse por vencido/a* = to give up, *dárselas de* = to act like/show off as",
    "Related: *dar* (base verb, \"to give\"), *dado* (die/dice, as a noun), *dadivoso/a* (generous)"
  ],
